288 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The instruction set for the 8-bit RISC processor is kept simple to ensure easy implementation and testing. It includes basic operations such as addition, subtraction, logical AND, logical OR, and data transfer between registers. Each instruction is represented by a unique opcode, which the control unit uses to identify and execute the required operation.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
289 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (1. REQUIREMENT ANALYSIS)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
290 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The 8-bit RISC processor requires essential hardware description modules to perform basic arithmetic and logical operations. The system must handle 8-bit wide data and support a minimal instruction set for operations such as addition, subtraction, logical AND, and OR. The design will include components such as the Arithmetic Logic Unit \(ALU\), register file, program counter, instruction memory, and control unit. The implementation will be carried out in Verilog HDL, simulated using appropriate software tools.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
