/E (4. VERILOG IMPLEMENTATION)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
294 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The processor is built in Verilog by creating separate modules for each part like the ALU, Program Counter, Registers, and Control Unit. Each module is connected to work together according to the instruction set. The opcodes are decoded to control the data flow and operations. Testbenches are used to check that each part and the whole processor work correctly in simulation.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
